---
import PlaygroundShell from '../../components/PlaygroundShell.astro';
import RangeField from '../../components/RangeField.astro';
---
<PlaygroundShell title="Top 10 from many shards" hint="Players are spread over shards. To build the global top 10, ask each shard for its top N and merge. How big does N have to be? Each result is tested on 100 different simulated boards of 4,000 players.">
  <ol class="how">
    <li>Spread players <b>by hash</b> with <b>N = 3</b> on 8 shards: it is <b>usually right</b>, and wrong on some boards, because a shard sometimes holds 4 of the real top 10. That makes a bug that only appears now and then.</li>
    <li>Spread players <b>by region</b>, where one region has stronger players: the real top 10 sit in <b>one shard</b>, so N = 3 returns only 3 of them. It fails on nearly every board.</li>
    <li>Set <b>N to 10</b>: always exact, with either spreading. Any player in the global top 10 is in the top 10 of their own shard, so each shard needs to send 10, and no more.</li>
  </ol>
  <div class="pg lbb" data-lbb>
    <div class="pg-row">
      <label>Shards <select class="pg-in" data-s><option value="4">4</option><option value="8" selected>8</option></select></label>
      <label>Players are spread <select class="pg-in" data-how>
        <option value="hash">by a hash of the player id</option>
        <option value="region" selected>by region (one strong region)</option>
      </select></label>
      <RangeField label="Each shard sends its top N" name="n" min="1" max="10" value="3" />
    </div>
    <div class="pg-grid">
      <div class="pg-box" data-b1><h3>Rows sent to the merging server</h3><span class="pg-mono" data-o1></span><span class="pg-note" data-n1></span></div>
      <div class="pg-box" data-b2><h3>Exact top 10 on</h3><span class="pg-mono" data-o2></span><span class="pg-note" data-n2></span></div>
      <div class="pg-box" data-b3><h3>Where the real top 10 live (board 1)</h3><span class="pg-mono" data-o3></span><span class="pg-note" data-n3></span></div>
    </div>
    <p class="pg-out" data-verdict aria-live="polite"></p>
    <p class="pg-note">Model: scores are random with a long tail, and ties go to the lower player id. In the region layout, region 0 has players whose scores are 1.6 times higher. A merge is exact only if all 10 of the real top players appear in the lists that the shards sent.</p>
  </div>
</PlaygroundShell>
<script>
  import { query } from '../../playground';
  document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-lbb]').forEach((root) => {
    const q = query(root);
    const BOARDS = 100; const PLAYERS = 4000; const REGIONS = 8;
    const SEED = 31;
    const TOP = 10; // the query asks for the top 10
    const MEAN_SCORE = 1000; // scores are exponential with mean 1000
    const STRONG_REGION = 1.6; // region 0 scores 1.6x higher, so its players crowd the top
    // linear congruential generator (Numerical Recipes constants)
    let seed = SEED; const rnd = () => ((seed = (seed * 1664525 + 1013904223) % 4294967296) / 4294967296);
    // Each board is the list of players sorted best first, with the region each belongs to.
    const boards = Array.from({ length: BOARDS }, () => {
      const list = Array.from({ length: PLAYERS }, (_, id) => { const region = id % REGIONS; const base = Math.floor(-Math.log(1 - rnd()) * MEAN_SCORE); return { id, region, score: region === 0 ? Math.floor(base * STRONG_REGION) : base }; });
      return list.sort((a, b) => b.score - a.score || a.id - b.id);
    });
    // integer hash (murmur3-style finalizer)
    const mix = (id: number) => { let h = Math.imul(id, 2654435761) >>> 0; h ^= h >>> 15; h = Math.imul(h, 2246822519) >>> 0; h ^= h >>> 13; return h >>> 0; }; // spreads the bits, so the shard does not just follow the id's last digits
    const shardOf = (p: { id: number; region: number }, s: number, how: string) => (how === 'region' ? p.region % s : mix(p.id) % s);
    function draw() {
      const s = Number(q<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-s]').value); const how = q<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-how]').value; const n = Number(q<HTMLInputElement>('[data-n]').value);
      q('[data-nval]').textContent = String(n);
      let exact = 0; let firstFound = 0; let spread: number[] = [];
      boards.forEach((b, i) => {
        const sent = new Set<number>(); const taken = new Array(s).fill(0);
        for (const p of b) { const k = shardOf(p, s, how); if (taken[k] < n) { taken[k]++; sent.add(p.id); } }
        const truth = b.slice(0, TOP); const found = truth.filter((p) => sent.has(p.id)).length;
        if (found === TOP) exact++;
        if (i === 0) { firstFound = found; spread = new Array(s).fill(0); truth.forEach((p) => spread[shardOf(p, s, how)]++); }
      });
      q('[data-o1]').textContent = `${s * n} rows`; q('[data-n1]').textContent = `${s} shards times ${n} each, to answer a query for ${TOP}`;
      q('[data-o2]').textContent = `${exact} of ${BOARDS} boards`; q('[data-n2]').textContent = `board 1: ${firstFound} of the real top ${TOP} were found`;
      q('[data-o3]').textContent = spread.map((c, i) => `shard ${i + 1}: ${c}`).filter((_, i) => spread[i] > 0).join(', ');
      q('[data-n3]').textContent = `the most on one shard: ${Math.max(...spread)}`;
      q<HTMLElement>('[data-b1]').style.setProperty('--c', 'var(--accent)');
      q<HTMLElement>('[data-b2]').style.setProperty('--c', exact === BOARDS ? 'var(--good)' : 'var(--bad)');
      q<HTMLElement>('[data-b3]').style.setProperty('--c', 'var(--accent)');
      const out = q('[data-verdict]'); const bad = exact < BOARDS; out.classList.toggle('bad', bad);
      out.textContent = exact === BOARDS ? (n >= TOP ? `Always exact, because any player in the global top ${TOP} is in the top ${TOP} of their own shard. Sending ${s * n} rows is the least that is always safe.` : `Exact on all ${BOARDS} boards with N = ${n}, but only because of how these boards happen to fall. A shard with more than ${n} of the real top 10 would break it.`)
        : `Wrong on ${BOARDS - exact} of ${BOARDS} boards: a shard held more of the real top ${TOP} than the ${n} it was asked for, so the merged list missed players. Asking each shard for ${TOP} is always right.`;
    }
    root.addEventListener('input', draw); root.addEventListener('change', draw);
    draw();
  });
</script>
